  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Fiji, the Pacific Horticultural and Agricultural Market Access Plus (PHAMA Plus) Program has supported three agribusinesses, Road King Farms, Kaiming Agro Processing and Lami Kava to continue to expand and diversify their export markets, collectively achieving additional export revenue of AUD2.73 million in FY2025. Their range of products include kava, ginger and taro. Road King Farms, a Taveuni-based agribusiness, entered the Australian export market in 2024. Support from PHAMA Plus helped the company revolutionize taro processing and export from the island community. For example, investments in new infrastructure have reduced waste, improved quality to meet biosecurity standards and provided farmers across the island better opportunities to sell more taro at higher prices. Road King Farm&#x2019;s success has also created new jobs, employing up to 70 people, 90% of whom are women.  Road King Farms received the Agribusiness Innovation Award at the Fiji&#x2019;s 2024 Prime Ministers International Business Awards.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHAMA Plus provided technical assistance to the Tongan Watermelon Export Taskforce to improve watermelon quality from the field to the packhouse, introducing improved harvesting techniques and heat management and cooling systems for storage. PHAMA Plus works closely with biosecurity authorities and shipping lines to support the timely and effective fumigation and coordination of shipping schedules, to protect quality and shelf life. In 2022, the value of watermelon exports has increased modestly from AUD 388,749 to AUD 486,823.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia and New Zealand funded Pacific Horticultural and Agricultural Program (PHAMA Plus) has supported Agri-businesses to develop and advance of the agricultural exports industry.  PHAMA Plus brokered the linkage between Cathliro, a female led Cocoa Agri-business, and Overseas Buyers, resulting in the continued growth of exports. Cathliro successfully maintained its business relationships with overseas buyers and achieved an additional export of 8,758kg of cocoa products to New Zealand. This export is valued at AUD67,750.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Twelve (12) women-led clusters on the island of Taveuni have started experimenting with organic ginger farming through PHAMA Plus partnership with Food Well Fiji Pte Ltd. This intervention aims to support up to 175 women farming households with the long-term objective of commercially growing and exporting ginger, a first for the island. PHAMA plus also integrated sustainable climate-friendly farming practices by encouraging the planting of vetiver grass for erosion management, sediment and pollution control and flood mitigation. Each cluster aims to produce 100tons of ginger at the end of the pilot phase to be sold through Food Well.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
